<code>assert word != null => \forall String prefix; this.startsWith(prefix) && this.keysWithPrefix(prefix).contains(word) == false;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert word != null => \forall String prefix; this.startsWith(prefix) && this.keysWithPrefix(prefix).contains(word) == false;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert word != null => \forall String prefix; this.startsWith(prefix) && this.keysWithPrefix(prefix).contains(word) => !this.keysWithPrefix(prefix).contains(word);</code>

However, the above assert statement can be simplified since `this.keysWithPrefix(prefix).contains(word)` would be false after the removal operation. Therefore, a more accurate and simpler assert statement would be:

<code>assert word != null => \forall String prefix; this.startsWith(prefix) && \old(this.keysWithPrefix(prefix)).contains(word) => !this.keysWithPrefix(prefix).contains(word);</code>

This ensures that if the word was present in any list of strings starting with each prefix before the removal, it will not be present in those lists after the removal.
--------------------
